    "### Cell Description\n",
    "\n",
    "This Python script prompts the user for the path to a main dataset folder and checks its validity. It assumes a dataset structure where images are stored in patient-specific subfolders, and the image files follow the nnUNet format.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Functionality:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **User Input**:\n",
    "   - The user is asked to input the path to the main dataset folder containing patient images (in `.nii` or `.nii.gz` format).\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Path Validation**:\n",
    "   - The script checks whether the entered path exists and is a valid directory. If not, it will print an error message and stop further execution.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Dataset Structure**:\n",
    "   - Upon finding a valid path, the script prints the expected folder structure:\n",
    "     ```\n",
    "     images/\n",
    "     ├── Patient_XXX/\n",
    "     │   └── Patient_XXX_000Y.nii\n",
    "     ```\n",
    "     where `000Y` represents the image channel identifier in the nnUNet format.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Listing Patient Folders**:\n",
    "   - The script lists all patient subfolders within the main dataset directory and prints how many patient folders are found, along with the list of patient IDs."
   ]
  },
