    "### Cell Description\n",
    "\n",
    "This Python script allows you to load and inspect the NIfTI files present in a patient folder. It provides detailed information about the files, such as their shape, data type, spacing, and slice thickness, for a preliminary analysis of the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Input Patient ID**:\n",
    "   - The user needs to enter the patient ID, which corresponds to the name of the folder.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Patient Folder Check**:\n",
    "   - The script verifies if the patient folder exists. If not, it prints an error message and stops.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **NIfTI File Search**:\n",
    "   - Inside the patient folder, the script looks for all files with `.nii` or `.nii.gz` extensions.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Loading and Inspecting Files**:\n",
    "   - For each NIfTI file found, the script attempts to load it using the `nibabel` library.\n",
    "   - It extracts and prints the following information:\n",
    "     - Image shape (shape).\n",
    "     - Data type of the image (dtype).\n",
    "     - Spacing between the voxels (spacing) for the first two dimensions (x, y).\n",
    "     - Slice thickness (slice thickness), if available.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Error Handling**:\n",
    "   - If a file cannot be loaded, an error message is displayed along with the exception description.\n",
    "\n",
    "This script is useful for exploring and obtaining general information about NIfTI data in a dataset, assisting in the data preparation and validation phase."
   ]
  },
